# Valgrind suppressions for the .github/workflows/valgrind.yml memcheck gate.
#
# Intentionally empty to start. Suppressions are grown EMPIRICALLY from the
# first real CI run's output rather than guessed up front -- guessing risks
# masking a genuine leak. When valgrind reports a known one-time libstdc++ /
# glibc internal allocation (e.g. locale/iostream init, dynamic-loader buffers)
# that is NOT a qwc leak, copy the `{ ... }` block valgrind prints with
# `--gen-suppressions=all` into this file, give it a descriptive name, and
# narrow it to the library frame so it can't hide a real qwc-side leak.
#
# Example shape (do not enable until observed in CI):
#
# {
#    libstdc++-locale-init-once
#    Memcheck:Leak
#    match-leak-kinds: reachable
#    ...
#    obj:*/libstdc++.so.*
# }
